1
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,350
Join us at Zhong An.

2
00:01:45,430 --> 00:01:46,710
Can we only use guns here?

3
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,040
Take a look at this.

4
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:07,510
You'll be deported over this piece of paper.

5
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:10,870
Whatever.

6
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:35,150
This all started because of Zhong An.

7
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:37,310
I won't just stand by and do nothing.

8
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:42,560
Through the local embassy,

9
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,630
I can help restore your Chinese citizenship.

10
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:47,680
That way, they won't be able to touch you.

11
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:53,800
The Silent Protectors operate in the dark,

12
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,000
and can never step into the light.

13
00:02:59,870 --> 00:03:00,870
Have you thought about this?

14
00:03:02,030 --> 00:03:03,470
Once you're deported,

15
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,310
all of your Silent Protectors

16
00:03:06,430 --> 00:03:07,910
will be driven out along with you.

17
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,190
Fine by me.

18
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:13,680
I'll hand them all over to you then,

19
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,150
to join Zhong An.

20
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:19,080
But only if they're willing.

21
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:25,400
Only when light and darkness coexist

22
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:29,080
can the world stay in balance.

23
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,080
Zhong An belongs to the light,

24
00:03:31,870 --> 00:03:33,520
and the Silent Protectors are the dark.

25
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,680
I'll handle this.

26
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,560
This style looks nice.

27
00:04:00,910 --> 00:04:02,190
Do you have other colors?

28
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:05,030
This one's nice.

29
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:10,310
This looks good.

30
00:04:11,870 --> 00:04:13,520
I think this one's great too.

31
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:15,870
Check this one out, too.

32
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,830
Come take a look!

33
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:22,560
Give me the stuff.

34
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:23,510
Have a look!

35
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,720
Hold onto your things.

36
00:04:25,950 --> 00:04:26,920
Come check it out!

37
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:43,510
Fresh fruit!

38
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:45,750
Come take a look!

39
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:48,000
Fresh fruit!

40
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,000
Have a look!

41
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:09,390
Hello, ma'am. What can I get you?

42
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:09,920
Coffee.

43
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:10,630
Right away.

44
00:06:11,510 --> 00:06:12,310
Thank you.

45
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,480
Take a look.

46
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,430
Looks like

47
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:54,310
you'll be defending a stateless person.

48
00:07:55,950 --> 00:07:57,000
In court,

49
00:07:57,510 --> 00:07:59,160
you won't suddenly get amnesia, will you?

50
00:08:01,070 --> 00:08:02,270
I can forget everything,

51
00:08:02,510 --> 00:08:04,750
except that I'm your comrade-in-arms.

52
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:09,270
Then I guess I'm pretty lucky.

53
00:08:09,870 --> 00:08:10,920
Don't worry.

54
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,910
Given that Zhong An Group,

55
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:23,320
as a representative of Chinese security companies,

56
00:09:23,910 --> 00:09:27,150
has made great contributions to our security work,

57
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,720
this serves only as a warning:

58
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:33,030
You must operate with respect for local laws.

59
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:36,080
A fine of 10,000 dirhams is imposed.

60
00:09:45,630 --> 00:09:47,870
Mr. Wei Tian has neither citizenship

61
00:09:47,870 --> 00:09:49,600
nor a local residence permit.

62
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:52,240
He openly flouted local laws

63
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:53,910
by defusing a bomb without authorization,

64
00:09:53,910 --> 00:09:55,270
and is considered a dangerous individual.

65
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:56,600
Notice is hereby given:

66
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:59,080
Mr. Wei Tian is ordered to leave Antilocaris

67
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,200
and may not re-enter.

68
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:02,150
This order takes effect tomorrow.

69
00:10:07,510 --> 00:10:08,480
Your Honor.

70
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:11,390
On behalf of my client, Mr. Wei Tian,

71
00:10:11,390 --> 00:10:12,390
I have a statement to make.

72
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:13,750
Proceed.

73
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,390
My client is innocent.

74
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:19,200
We request his immediate release.

75
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,510
State your grounds.

76
00:10:26,510 --> 00:10:27,320
First.

77
00:10:27,670 --> 00:10:29,550
The rescued employees of Shida Telecom

78
00:10:29,550 --> 00:10:30,870
are all Chinese citizens.

79
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:33,600
When Chinese citizens in another country

80
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,080
encounter a terrorist attack,

81
00:10:35,790 --> 00:10:38,360
under the Purposes in Chapter I of the UN Charter:

82
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:41,320
to maintain international peace and security,

83
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:44,390
and to that end, take effective collective measures

84
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:48,120
for the prevention and removal of threats to peace,

85
00:10:48,910 --> 00:10:52,080
suppress acts of aggression or other breaches of peace,

86
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:53,790
and by peaceful means,

87
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,790
in conformity with principles of justice and international law,

88
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,600
adjust or settle disputes

89
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:02,080
or situations which might lead to a breach of peace.

90
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,390
My client, Mr. Wei Tian,

91
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:09,360
risked his own life to defuse the bomb.

92
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:13,870
The people he saved were not local citizens.

93
00:11:14,550 --> 00:11:17,320
His action caused no harm to this country;

94
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,440
on the contrary, it was beneficial.

95
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:22,390
Is this truly a violation of local laws?

96
00:11:24,510 --> 00:11:25,320
Second.

97
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,000
The ruling states

98
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:30,080
that the defendant failed to observe local laws

99
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:31,870
and fulfill his duty to assist the police.

100
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:35,120
Everything my client did

101
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:38,000
was because the police failed to arrive in time,

102
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:40,000
and under urgent circumstances,

103
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:42,120
his actions were a defense of necessity.

104
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:45,960
Is a defense of necessity also illegal?

105
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:49,000
Third, the ruling also states

106
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,670
that had the bomb defusal failed,

107
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:53,150
would it have put local residents in danger?

108
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:56,870
But had the defusal failed,

109
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:58,270
wouldn't my client

110
00:11:58,360 --> 00:12:01,320
have risked his own life as well?

111
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:03,630
Yet facts have proven

112
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,080
that his action was right.

113
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,390
Not only did he save the employees,

114
00:12:06,390 --> 00:12:08,870
he also prevented local residents

115
00:12:09,030 --> 00:12:10,670
from facing the same danger.

116
00:12:11,030 --> 00:12:13,030
Yet you turn around and blame him!

117
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:15,390
Fourth.

118
00:12:15,790 --> 00:12:18,080
Under the Convention Relating to the Status of Stateless Persons,

119
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:20,240
pursuant to Article 31, Paragraph 1,

120
00:12:20,550 --> 00:12:22,870
Contracting States shall not, save on grounds of national security

121
00:12:22,870 --> 00:12:24,510
or public order,

122
00:12:24,670 --> 00:12:26,600
expel a stateless person

123
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,270
lawfully in their territory.

124
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,870
Even if deportation is warranted,

125
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:32,960
under Article 31, Paragraph 3,

126
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:36,000
Contracting States shall allow such a stateless person

127
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,360
a reasonable period

128
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,720
to obtain legal admission

129
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,200
into another country.

130
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,510
Upon verification,

131
00:12:41,670 --> 00:12:44,630
your country is a contracting party to the convention.

132
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:48,150
Therefore, this ruling clearly violates

133
00:12:48,150 --> 00:12:49,630
the terms of the international convention.

134
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,270
It fails to reasonably safeguard

135
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:52,960
the interests of stateless persons,

136
00:12:53,150 --> 00:12:56,000
and severely infringes upon their rights.

137
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:00,080
Lastly, I would like to add one more point.

138
00:13:00,790 --> 00:13:03,240
Although my client is stateless,

139
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:04,910
he has consistently performed

140
00:13:04,910 --> 00:13:06,600
charitable deeds in the local community.

141
00:13:07,150 --> 00:13:09,240
He rescued girls from local tribes,

142
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:12,910
sparing them from being sold and persecuted.

143
00:13:13,630 --> 00:13:16,030
He has continuously aided local refugees.

144
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:17,320
What he has brought to the local people

145
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:19,320
is a positive impact.

146
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,120
If he is expelled

147
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,630
merely because of his status,

148
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:26,150
it could bring upon this city

149
00:13:26,150 --> 00:13:27,960
a very terrible reputation.

150
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,720
Do you think we stand a chance?

151
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:34,030
I think we should discuss this further.

152
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:34,840
What do you say?

153
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:37,510
We must be cautious. This is no small matter.

154
00:13:37,510 --> 00:13:38,270
All right.

155
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,870
Court is adjourned for 30 minutes.

156
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:05,320
Don't worry. It'll be fine.

157
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:06,550
I'm not worried.

158
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,870
Rosie's so amazing.

159
00:14:10,630 --> 00:14:13,120
Who knew the Silent Protectors were full of surprises?

160
00:14:13,870 --> 00:14:15,750
You think we're all as shallow as you?

161
00:14:16,750 --> 00:14:18,750
But I heard someone only knows how to

162
00:14:18,750 --> 00:14:20,200
hide behind the Silent Protectors

163
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,960
and never dares to face the enemy head-on.

164
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:23,790
That's because I'm a technician.

165
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:58,390
Given the legal dispute over unauthorized bomb defusal,

166
00:14:58,510 --> 00:15:00,720
after deliberation, this court announces

167
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:02,390
that Mr. Wei Tian is not guilty.

168
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:19,870
Anda.

169
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:20,720
Wei Tian.

170
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:23,360
What's the occasion? Why all this food?

171
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,390
Who made it?

172
00:15:25,390 --> 00:15:26,600
I'm so glad you came.

173
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:27,000
Here.

174
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:29,720
Try some first.

175
00:15:29,910 --> 00:15:30,440
Taste it.

176
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:35,240
Just from the smell,

177
00:15:35,670 --> 00:15:37,510
it's like Captain's cooking.

178
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,320
It tastes almost the same.

179
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:44,600
I tried my best to cook all these dishes,

180
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,960
but only these few turned out well.

181
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,750
In the future, I'll work even harder

182
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:51,120
to make food you like.

183
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:57,550
Wei Tian, if anything happens in the future,

184
00:15:57,670 --> 00:15:59,390
can you let me know first?

185
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,270
When the judge was announcing the verdict,

186
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:02,750
do you know how nervous I was?

187
00:16:02,750 --> 00:16:04,840
I thought I'd never see you again.

188
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,750
Do... Do you have any idea

189
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,550
how much you mean to me?

190
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:19,000
In the past,

191
00:16:21,390 --> 00:16:22,720
I had a woman I truly loved.

192
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,440
She cooked for me, too.

193
00:16:25,270 --> 00:16:26,600
The taste of her cooking

194
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:30,000
will always be the best to me.

195
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,080
I'll never forget it.

196
00:16:33,030 --> 00:16:35,910
And I only see you as a sister.

197
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:41,960
Then... have you ever thought of trying something new?

198
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,750
Let's just eat. Come on.

199
00:17:32,750 --> 00:17:33,200
Here.

200
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:35,640
Hold onto this flag.

201
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:37,790
When the Red Team comes out later,

202
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:39,550
wave this and cheer them on.

203
00:17:43,110 --> 00:17:44,070
I'll go make a call.

204
00:18:04,310 --> 00:18:06,880
Look, those men will run up from over there.

205
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:07,880
Make sure to cheer them on.

206
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,270
Okay, Mom.

207
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,680
When the Red Team plays in a bit,

208
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:22,680
cheer for them.

209
00:18:24,790 --> 00:18:25,510
Have some water.

210
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:30,830
Take it slow.

211
00:18:39,590 --> 00:18:40,400
Look,

212
00:18:43,270 --> 00:18:44,680
do you think the Red Team can win?

213
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:55,880
Your daughter is so adorable.

214
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,750
I couldn't help taking a photo of her.

215
00:18:59,030 --> 00:18:59,830
Thank you.

216
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:03,240
You are too. Very beautiful.

217
00:19:10,030 --> 00:19:11,480
The weather is wonderful today.

218
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:17,070
I won't disturb you anymore. Good luck!

219
00:19:47,110 --> 00:19:48,240
Wei Tian, where are you?

220
00:19:48,350 --> 00:19:49,000
What is it?

221
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:51,160
It's nothing.

222
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:52,960
You'd better hurry back.

223
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:53,920
I'll tell you when you get back.

224
00:19:54,070 --> 00:19:55,440
All right, I'm on my way back.

225
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:11,790
Come on!

226
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:15,400
Aren't those guys great?

227
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,310
Go, Red Team!

228
00:20:16,310 --> 00:20:17,110
Is it fun to watch?

229
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,240
Run!

230
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:58,240
Go!

231
00:21:22,790 --> 00:21:25,310
How's that, Wei Tian? Enjoying the fireworks?

232
00:21:25,310 --> 00:21:26,200
Hades.

233
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:27,960
What a shame.

234
00:21:28,550 --> 00:21:31,200
I didn't let you enjoy one last family reunion.

235
00:21:31,830 --> 00:21:35,000
Though keeping you alive is the greatest torture.

236
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:37,310
Why are you doing this?

237
00:21:41,030 --> 00:21:44,200
Wei Tian, the game has only just begun.

238
00:22:02,350 --> 00:22:03,790
I still remember you saying

239
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:07,750
that the beauty of a single flower and a bouquet

240
00:22:08,070 --> 00:22:09,200
are just the same.

241
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:13,000
Wherever they come from, that's where they belong.

242
00:22:14,110 --> 00:22:15,790
I've found Hades.

243
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:17,030
Don't worry.

244
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:20,200
Once I settle the score with him,

245
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:23,480
I'll definitely take you and Qiaoqiao back to China.

246
00:22:24,830 --> 00:22:26,350
The weather's been nice lately.

247
00:22:27,070 --> 00:22:29,720
The jacarandas in Antilocaris are in bloom.

248
00:22:30,270 --> 00:22:32,750
I'll bring some for you to see in a few days.

249
00:23:30,590 --> 00:23:33,070
Why do you think I keep having hallucinations lately?

250
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:36,350
What did you see?

251
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:39,400
I just keep feeling like...

252
00:23:39,590 --> 00:23:41,110
someone's watching me from behind.

253
00:23:43,830 --> 00:23:45,070
Don't scare me.

254
00:23:45,550 --> 00:23:47,830
Hallucinations are also tied to amnesia.

255
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:49,720
They might actually help

256
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:50,960
trigger your memories.

257
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:51,680
Really?

258
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:54,160
There's also another possibility:

259
00:23:54,270 --> 00:23:56,200
you're dizzy from hunger,

260
00:23:56,350 --> 00:23:57,550
or thirsty,

261
00:23:57,590 --> 00:23:59,200
or dazed by the sun just now.

262
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:00,720
Any of those can cause hallucinations.

263
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,000
I'm guessing it's just the heat.

264
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:04,200
By the way,

265
00:24:04,790 --> 00:24:06,720
the court's ruling on our case

266
00:24:07,030 --> 00:24:09,000
has made the Silent Protectors quite famous.

267
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:10,640
So going forward,

268
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:12,160
we might not have as much freedom.

269
00:24:13,440 --> 00:24:15,000
You're the one who needs to be most careful.

270
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:17,480
Because you're in constant danger.

271
00:24:17,750 --> 00:24:18,880
We all need to be careful.

272
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:24,880
Why don't you try hallucinating some more?

273
00:24:25,110 --> 00:24:26,030
Get out of here.

274
00:24:26,270 --> 00:24:27,750
Captain, stop teasing me.

275
00:24:29,110 --> 00:24:30,350
It's so hot.

276
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:09,270
Sha Lan.

277
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:10,510
What are you doing?

278
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:12,030
I think we should replace our

279
00:26:12,030 --> 00:26:13,110
Wi-Fi range extender.

280
00:26:13,270 --> 00:26:15,000
Why is uploading videos such a hassle?

281
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:16,720
Delete it right now.

282
00:26:17,240 --> 00:26:19,680
Rosie, why are you so nervous?

283
00:26:20,310 --> 00:26:21,350
I was just thinking,

284
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:24,200
if I upload this video online,

285
00:26:24,270 --> 00:26:25,480
maybe it could help you recover

286
00:26:25,480 --> 00:26:26,550
your past memories.

287
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:28,920
Even though you don't remember much,

288
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:30,680
someone out there definitely remembers you.

289
00:26:32,110 --> 00:26:33,440
Would someone really remember me?

290
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:38,720
That's impossible.

291
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:40,110
If someone remembered me,

292
00:26:40,110 --> 00:26:41,400
they'd have come looking for me long ago.

293
00:26:42,070 --> 00:26:42,590
Delete it.

294
00:26:42,790 --> 00:26:43,880
Rosie,

295
00:26:45,110 --> 00:26:45,960
what if

296
00:26:46,070 --> 00:26:47,030
they really do remember you,

297
00:26:47,030 --> 00:26:48,590
but just don't know where to find you?

298
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:50,960
If they see this video,

299
00:26:51,310 --> 00:26:52,750
they might even reach out to me.

300
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:53,920
Trust me.

301
00:27:45,270 --> 00:27:46,480
Tomorrow morning at ten,

302
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:48,590
the target will appear in the Blue District.

303
00:27:49,310 --> 00:27:50,350
Prepare to shoot to kill.

304
00:28:19,550 --> 00:28:20,640
One, two, one!

305
00:28:21,590 --> 00:28:22,720
One, two, one!

306
00:28:23,550 --> 00:28:24,680
One, two, one!

307
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:25,920
Keep up, everyone!

308
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:30,200
One, two, one!

309
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:32,350
Look, look!

310
00:28:35,160 --> 00:28:35,790
Anda!

311
00:28:40,750 --> 00:28:41,550
Let's go, let's go.

312
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:44,550
I... We know each other.

313
00:28:45,160 --> 00:28:45,960
My old classmate, Anda.

314
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,480
You really don't remember me?

315
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:53,790
We've met before.

316
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,680
Or to be exact, I've seen you.

317
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:57,030
Back in 2014,

318
00:28:57,030 --> 00:28:58,640
during training at the Institute of International Relations,

319
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:04,160
you were in that class.

320
00:29:04,160 --> 00:29:04,640
Right.

321
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:08,550
Let me reintroduce myself.

322
00:29:08,750 --> 00:29:10,960
I'm from the Africa branch of Zhong An Security,

323
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:11,590
Xiang Bei.

324
00:29:13,270 --> 00:29:14,510
So you've been hiding here all along.

325
00:29:14,510 --> 00:29:15,310
Why didn't you say so earlier?

326
00:29:15,510 --> 00:29:17,350
Well, we've got plenty of time ahead, right?

327
00:29:18,110 --> 00:29:19,550
Now that I've introduced myself,

328
00:29:19,830 --> 00:29:20,550
I'll get back to work.

329
00:29:40,110 --> 00:29:41,110
Did you see that?

330
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:44,070
Why are you showing me this?

331
00:29:44,590 --> 00:29:45,830
You know I don't trade stocks.

332
00:29:46,790 --> 00:29:48,000
I wanted to share with you

333
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:49,200
the secret to making money.

334
00:29:50,590 --> 00:29:53,160
The Silent Protectors saved the girls of our tribe.

335
00:29:53,480 --> 00:29:54,590
I'm deeply grateful.

336
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:55,880
Consider this a gift

337
00:29:56,070 --> 00:29:56,720
for all of you.

338
00:29:58,480 --> 00:29:59,790
I appreciate the thought.

339
00:30:01,030 --> 00:30:02,310
I have another small gift.

340
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:04,400
My sixth sense tells me

341
00:30:04,790 --> 00:30:05,830
you might run into some

342
00:30:05,830 --> 00:30:07,200
trouble and danger soon.

343
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:09,510
Make sure you stay safe.

344
00:30:13,270 --> 00:30:14,640
Actually, we Silent Protectors

345
00:30:15,030 --> 00:30:16,790
have always lived in bloodshed.

346
00:30:17,270 --> 00:30:19,000
There's never really been safety for us.

347
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:22,270
Don't brush it off.

348
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:23,790
I'm serious.

349
00:31:26,830 --> 00:31:27,440
Wei Tian!

350
00:31:29,790 --> 00:31:30,830
I knew it.

351
00:31:30,920 --> 00:31:32,590
I felt like someone was following me.

352
00:31:32,750 --> 00:31:33,960
Turns out it's you.

353
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:36,960
Since you're here,

354
00:31:36,960 --> 00:31:37,680
tell me what you think.

355
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:38,680
How does this dress look?

356
00:31:38,830 --> 00:31:39,680
It's very pretty.

357
00:31:40,590 --> 00:31:41,830
I'm going to try this on.

358
00:31:41,830 --> 00:31:42,590
Sure.

359
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:44,720
What a coincidence.

360
00:32:31,550 --> 00:32:32,200
Are you okay?

361
00:32:33,160 --> 00:32:33,680
What's wrong?

362
00:33:11,830 --> 00:33:12,510
Excuse me.

363
00:33:13,070 --> 00:33:13,480
Hello.

364
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:14,790
Do you have white shoes here?

365
00:33:15,200 --> 00:33:16,350
Sorry, we don't.

366
00:33:31,550 --> 00:33:32,550
Rosie! Rosie!

367
00:33:32,550 --> 00:33:33,480
The white shoes.

368
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:35,790
What are you doing?

369
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,200
I need to find the white shoes.

370
00:33:37,480 --> 00:33:38,160
The white shoes.

371
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:39,160
Let go of me!

372
00:33:55,640 --> 00:33:57,240
Someone is trying to assassinate Rosie.

373
00:33:59,750 --> 00:34:00,550
This person,

374
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:03,550
I think,

375
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:06,960
knows Rosie's routine very well,

376
00:34:08,480 --> 00:34:09,280
and

377
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:11,280
has been tailing her for a while.

378
00:34:18,510 --> 00:34:19,360
I think

379
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:22,960
the enemy isn't just after Rosie.

380
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:25,960
Because during the operation that day,

381
00:34:26,030 --> 00:34:27,840
you were with Rosie.

382
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:55,280
What... What's wrong?

383
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:57,880
I... I'll go find them.

384
00:34:58,030 --> 00:34:58,840
Don't go.

385
00:34:59,590 --> 00:35:00,710
They can't find out.

386
00:35:01,440 --> 00:35:03,280
They can't... They can't find out.

387
00:35:21,480 --> 00:35:23,110
Did you remember something else?

388
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:53,710
What's wrong with her?

389
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:56,960
She...

390
00:36:57,320 --> 00:36:58,320
First thing in the morning,

391
00:36:58,320 --> 00:36:59,510
why did you bring me out here?

392
00:36:59,670 --> 00:37:01,230
I still have so much work to do.

393
00:37:02,070 --> 00:37:04,630
Why is work all you ever think about?

394
00:37:04,760 --> 00:37:06,840
Can't you enjoy life a little?

395
00:37:07,710 --> 00:37:08,150
Come on.

396
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:09,150
I've got a surprise for you.

397
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:15,920
Didn't you say Rosie shouldn't come out?

398
00:37:16,510 --> 00:37:17,440
Lure the snake out.

399
00:37:19,070 --> 00:37:20,190
Isn't that dangerous?

400
00:37:21,110 --> 00:37:22,280
You and I are here.

401
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:25,840
Hello, my goddess.

402
00:37:25,840 --> 00:37:27,150
Long time no see.

403
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:28,840
Didn't we just see each other?

404
00:37:28,840 --> 00:37:29,320
Here, give it to me.

405
00:37:29,320 --> 00:37:30,880
I was talking about Rosie.

406
00:37:33,230 --> 00:37:34,510
Can you be serious?

407
00:37:35,230 --> 00:37:36,920
What I asked you to do yesterday,

408
00:37:37,030 --> 00:37:37,960
hurry up and hand it over.

409
00:37:38,400 --> 00:37:39,630
What's the rush?

410
00:37:40,030 --> 00:37:40,510
Rosie.

411
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:41,590
Wait for me.

412
00:37:42,070 --> 00:37:43,000
All right, go on.

413
00:37:43,280 --> 00:37:44,150
Take your time.

414
00:37:44,710 --> 00:37:45,280
Wait for me!

415
00:37:47,960 --> 00:37:50,190
What are you two up to?

416
00:37:51,190 --> 00:37:52,440
You'll find out in a bit.

417
00:37:56,670 --> 00:37:57,960
Coming!

418
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:17,190
These coffee beans...

419
00:38:17,190 --> 00:38:18,150
are selected from five countries,

420
00:38:18,150 --> 00:38:20,110
five of the finest coffee beans.

421
00:38:20,630 --> 00:38:21,760
You've got to try it.

422
00:38:35,190 --> 00:38:36,000
These coffee beans

423
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:37,840
require exceptionally good water.

424
00:38:38,280 --> 00:38:39,400
This mineral water,

425
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:41,280
I had it flown in specially.

426
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:42,320
Brewing coffee with it

427
00:38:42,510 --> 00:38:44,190
makes it taste amazing.

428
00:39:24,920 --> 00:39:25,710
Go on, try it.

429
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:27,400
See if it tastes familiar.

430
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:50,710
It's really good.

431
00:39:51,360 --> 00:39:53,440
The sweet spring water and bitter coffee

432
00:39:53,920 --> 00:39:55,840
give it a taste of happiness.

433
00:40:03,190 --> 00:40:03,630
Move, hurry!

434
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:17,840
Rosie!

435
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:18,840
Rosie!

436
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:21,670
Are you okay?

437
00:40:26,920 --> 00:40:27,440
Hurry!

438
00:40:34,670 --> 00:40:35,880
Let's go, come on.

439
00:40:37,590 --> 00:40:38,670
What about me?

440
00:40:39,030 --> 00:40:39,840
Sha Lan.

441
00:40:40,670 --> 00:40:41,440
You guys go back first.

442
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:41,670
Okay.

443
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:42,190
Go, go!

444
00:40:42,480 --> 00:40:43,030
Move!

445
00:41:18,880 --> 00:41:19,440
Captain.

446
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:23,190
It's a really tricky angle,

447
00:41:23,590 --> 00:41:26,920
and today has the lowest wind speed in days.

448
00:41:27,440 --> 00:41:29,000
In and out without a trace.

449
00:41:29,150 --> 00:41:30,230
They moved fast.

450
00:41:50,880 --> 00:41:52,070
In my experience,

451
00:41:52,190 --> 00:41:54,150
this is a well-trained killer.

452
00:41:56,070 --> 00:41:57,710
But for some reason,

453
00:41:57,710 --> 00:41:59,360
the moment he went to pull the trigger,

454
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:00,960
he hesitated.

455
00:42:05,230 --> 00:42:06,030
Find him.

456
00:43:07,480 --> 00:43:09,000
Rosie, think about it.

457
00:43:09,510 --> 00:43:10,480
Lately,

458
00:43:10,670 --> 00:43:11,630
who have you seen?

459
00:43:12,070 --> 00:43:13,550
Has anyone contacted you?

460
00:43:15,550 --> 00:43:17,510
No one out of the ordinary.

461
00:43:18,150 --> 00:43:19,670
Think carefully again.

462
00:43:19,920 --> 00:43:20,880
Really no one?

463
00:43:23,480 --> 00:43:23,960
Oh, wait.

464
00:43:24,510 --> 00:43:25,880
I met Grace the other day.

465
00:43:26,110 --> 00:43:27,590
She recommended a stock to me.

466
00:43:34,190 --> 00:43:34,760
This one right here.
